  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Matrices and Transformations: finding an object from its image</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.1: Find the inverse of a matrix and use it to find the object of a given image point.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 14, Section 4.1 and Exercise B, Question 5 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: inverse found by formula and used to recover an object point, new matrices, randomised, with named and follow-through feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
